        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Shahnameh</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 977 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Ferdowsi, Persian poet of Tus, who worked on it for 33 years; it takes in about 1,000 verses by Daqiqi, an earlier poet at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanid Empire</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">Epic poem in Early New Persian of some 50,000 rhyming couplets (distichs), in 62 stories and 990 chapters, in three ages: mythical, heroic and historical</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where it is now</span><span class="info-stat-val">Read in print, notably in Djalal Khaleghi-Motlagh's critical edition; early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> include the 1217 copy rediscovered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> and the 1276 manuscript of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-museum">British Museum</a>; the illustrated Baysonghori Shahnameh of 1430 is at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golestan-palace">Golestan Palace</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rostam">Rostam</a> and Sohrab; the Seven Stages of Rostam; Zal and Rudaba; Zahhak and Kaveh the blacksmith; the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a>; illustrated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-miniature">Persian miniature</a> painting; its place in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-language">Persian language</a></span></div>
